SUMMARY:Tom Rosenstiel: How the Press Must Change to Save Democracy
DTSTART:20261023T003000Z
DTEND:20261023T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20260901T110827Z
UID:6af27669-3cb0-5ecd-b284-6ed085d62a2c
DESCRIPTION:The crisis in journalism\, says veteran journalist and media c
 ritic Tom Rosenstiel\, reflects a crisis in American democracy. Faith in n
 ews outlets has dwindled\, news deserts are expanding\, and audiences are 
 turning away from alarmist\, partisan\, and fragmented coverage. \nIn his
  new book The Next Journalism\, Rosenstiel argues that the roots of journa
 lism’s failure are intellectual\, not just financial or technological. H
 e outlines ten fundamental ways journalism must change to become more usef
 ul\, trustworthy\, and collaborative with the communities it serves.\n\nMo
 re info & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-10-22/tom-
 rosenstiel-how-press-must-change-save-democracy-0
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, 110 The Embarcade
 ro\, San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-10-22/tom-rosenstiel-how-
 press-must-change-save-democracy-0
END:VEVENT
